course: dictionary
lesson: 11333
title: The word you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word «you» is a pronoun. A pronoun takes the place of a name, so you do not have to say the name again. «You» means the person or people someone is talking to. When your teacher says, «You can sit by the window», the word «you» points at you.
explain: «You» can also mean anyone at all. Look at this rule: «You should brush your teeth twice a day». Here «you» does not mean one special person. It means everybody. Ask yourself: who is the rule for? The answer is anyone who reads it.
explain: Words change with place and with the kind of talk. In casual talk people write «u» or «ya» for you, and «thank ya» for «thank you». Many places have their own plural for more than one person, such as «you guys» in the USA or «you lot» in the UK. Formal writing, like an exam, avoids «you» and says «the candidate» instead.
fact: «You» is a pronoun, a word that stands in for a name.
fact: «You» can mean one person, a group of people, or people in general.
fact: In casual texts, «you» is often written as «u» or «ya», as in «c u l8r», which means see you later.
fact: Other places have their own plural words: «y'all» (US South), «youse» (Ireland, Australia, New Zealand), «you guys» (USA), «you lot» (UK).
fact: In a formal exam, writers avoid «you» and use «the candidate», «one», or the passive.
exercise: In «You can't get burnt when it's cloudy», who does «you» mean? | A farmer | *The person the big sister is talking to | The big sister herself | The cloud
exercise: In «Almost everything you touch was designed by someone», what does «you» mean? | *Anyone at all, people in general | The designer | A teacher | One special named person
exercise: Which word is a casual way to write «you» in a text? | *u | yourself | yours
test: Which phrase is a casual way of saying «thank you»? | *thank ya | thank yourselves | thank yours
test: In the rule «You should brush your teeth twice a day», who should brush their teeth? | Only one named child | Only the teacher | Only the dentist | *Anyone who reads the rule
exam: Which sentence is in the formal exam style? | u must check ur answers | youse must check the answers | you must check your answers | *the candidate must check the answers
